      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-42554",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/63/630aa5f44631094bc058347b09467e9dab2774274b219708ebd6af4e9bcfb855.png)\n\nThe figure above shows a gaming board whose inner circle has a radius of $1in$. The outer circle has a radius of $9in$ while the sides of the square have a length of $3in$. A player aims a dart at the board. Assuming that the dart lands on a random position inside the board, what is the probability that it will land inside the square but outside the inner circle? Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
