      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-5517",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/5f/5f65ead37d69f200a6054017b10a9e5d10a7ed2f357295cce7069dfe3131c457.png)\n\nA bullseye target is represented by a circle of radius $1$ contained inside a circle of radius $5$. An archer aims an arrow at the target. Assuming that the arrow lands on a random position inside the target, what is the probability of an archer missing the bullseye?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
